  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-41302-IP24-CYP101</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41302" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Labour Organization (ILO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Expertise of Ministry of labour&apos;s officials and of social partners is enhanced in the field of the financial , economic and fiscal sustainability of the national social security systems</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since 2018, the ILO has been engaged with the Health Insurance Organization (HIO) in Cyprus to provide technical assistance in the context of implementing the newly established General Healthcare System (GHS).  A project is being implemented which contributes to the improved long-term financial sustainability of the GHS, as well as sustained capacity of the institution to conduct actuarial valuation studies in the future.
In addition, the ILO and the Ministry of Labour and Social Insurance (MLSI), have been engaged in a long-standing technical collaboration for more than 50 years in the area of social protection.  A second project aims at supporting the MLSI in the reform of the national Social Protection System.
A third project with the Ministry of Finance is supporting the Cyprus Statistical Service for national accounts statistical disclosure and the Treasury for the public sector accounting standard disclosure with respect to the pension benefits under the General Social Insurance Scheme (GSIS).
Ultimately this work, through these projects, will lead to increased confidence and trust in the social security scheme of Cyprus, enhancing coverage, adequacy of benefits and financial sustainability over the long term.</narrative>
  </description>
